🧠 LIBRARY MANAGEMENT SYSTEM — FULL VIVA BREAKDOWN
1. 📦 Import
import java.util.*;
📌 Overall meaning:

Imports all utility classes like Scanner and ArrayList.

🧩 Terms:
import → includes external package
java.util → utility package
* → imports all classes
⭐ Alternatives:
import java.util.Scanner;
import java.util.ArrayList;
2. 📘 Book Class
class Book
📌 Overall meaning:

Creates blueprint for book objects.

🧩 Terms:
class → blueprint
Book → user-defined class
3. 🔢 Variables
int id;
String title;
boolean isIssued;
static int totalBooks = 0;
📌 Overall meaning:

Stores book details and library count.

🧩 Terms:
int → whole number
String → text
boolean → true/false
static → shared among all objects
⭐ Important: static

👉 totalBooks is shared by all books, not individual.

⭐ Alternatives:
Without static → each object has its own count (wrong for total tracking)
4. 🏗️ Constructor
Book(int id, String title)
📌 Overall meaning:

Initializes book when object is created.

🧩 Terms:
constructor → same name as class
this → refers to current object
⭐ Alternatives:
default constructor + setters
overloaded constructors (already used style)
5. 📥 issueBook()
if (!isIssued)
📌 Overall meaning:

Checks if book is available, then issues it.

🧩 Terms:
! → NOT operator
isIssued → boolean flag
⭐ Alternatives:
using enum status (AVAILABLE/ISSUED)
6. 🔄 returnBook()
📌 Overall meaning:

Marks book as returned.

⭐ Alternatives:
remove book from issued list (not ideal here)
7. 🖨️ display()
(isIssued ? "Issued" : "Available")
📌 Overall meaning:

Shows book status using ternary operator.

🧩 Terms:
? : → ternary operator
condition ? true : false
⭐ Alternatives:
if-else instead of ternary
8. 📊 static method
static void showTotalBooks()
📌 Overall meaning:

Shows total books in library.

🧩 Terms:
static → belongs to class, not object
⭐ Alternatives:
non-static method (but requires object)
9. 🚀 Main Class
public class LibrarySystem
📌 Overall meaning:

Runs entire program.

10. 📥 Scanner
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
⭐ Alternatives:

BufferedReader

11. 📚 ArrayList
ArrayList<Book> library = new ArrayList<>();
📌 Overall meaning:

Stores all books dynamically.

🧩 Terms:
ArrayList → dynamic list
<Book> → generics type safety
⭐ Alternatives:
LinkedList
array Book[]
12. 🔁 do-while loop
📌 Overall meaning:

Keeps menu running until exit.

⭐ Alternatives:
while(true) + break
13. 📋 Menu system
switch(choice)
📌 Overall meaning:

Selects operation based on user input.

⭐ Alternatives:
if-else ladder
14. ➕ Add Book
Book b = new Book(id, title);
library.add(b);
📌 Overall meaning:

Creates and stores book.

⭐ Alternatives:
using setter methods
15. 📤 Issue Book
for (Book book : library)
📌 Overall meaning:

Loops through all books.

🧩 Terms:
enhanced for loop
: means “in”
⭐ Alternatives:
normal for loop
iterator
16. 🔍 Search logic
if (book.id == issueId)
📌 Overall meaning:

Finds book by ID.

⭐ Alternatives:
using HashMap (faster search)
17. 📊 Static method call
Book.showTotalBooks();
📌 Overall meaning:

Calls class-level method.

⭐ Alternatives:
object-based call (not recommended for static)
18. 🚪 Exit
while (choice != 6);
📌 Overall meaning:

Stops program when user chooses exit.

🧠 OVERALL FLOW

👉 User opens menu
👉 Adds books
👉 Issues or returns books
👉 Views list
👉 Checks total books
👉 Exits program

⚡ CONCEPTUAL VIVA QUESTIONS (VERY IMPORTANT)
❓ What is static variable?

👉 Shared variable among all objects.

❓ Why totalBooks is static?

👉 Because it tracks total count of all books, not individual book.

❓ What is encapsulation here?

👉 Data is grouped inside class (Book).

❓ Why use ArrayList?

👉 Because size of library is dynamic.

❓ Difference between Array and ArrayList?

👉 Array = fixed size
👉 ArrayList = dynamic size

❓ Why use enhanced for loop?

👉 Easy to read and iterate collections.

❓ What is ternary operator?

👉 Shortcut of if-else.

❓ Why use class Book?

👉 To represent real-world entity (book).

❓ What happens if book not found?

👉 Program prints “Book not found”.

❓ Why use Scanner?

👉 To take user input.

❓ What is object in this program?

👉 Each Book created using new Book().

❓ What is method overloading/usage here?

👉 Constructor overloading concept used.

❓ Why break is used in loop?

👉 To stop searching once book is found.

❓ What is real-world use?

👉 Library management systems in schools and colleges.

🧠 FINAL ONE-LINE SUMMARY

“This program demonstrates OOP concepts like class, object, constructor, static variable, ArrayList, and menu-driven logic to simulate a library management system with issue, return, and tracking features.”
